```typescript
if (def.responseSchema && apiClient.getValidateResponse()) {
  const result = def.responseSchema.safeParse(responseBody);
  if (!result.success) {
    throw new EsiValidationError(
      `${apiClient.getLink()}/${path}`,
      result.error,
    );
  }
  responseBody = result.data;
}
```

So validation only happens when:
1. The endpoint definition has a `responseSchema`
2. The `apiClient.getValidateResponse()` returns `true`
I need to check whether `getValidateResponse()` is enabled by default or if it requires explicit configuration.

